title: Young Plan
new-page: true
subtitle: A new agreement on reparations
tags: event
view-if: year = 1929 and month >= 7 and in_right_coalition = 0 and young_plan_seen = 0 and not dnvp_toleration
on-arrival: young_plan_seen = 1; prussia_dnvp -= 0.1; prussia_nsdap += 0.1
go-to: young_plan_right_coalition if (in_right_coalition or dnvp_toleration); young_plan_normal if (in_right_coalition == 0 and dnvp_toleration == 0) 
max-visits: 1

@young_plan_normal

= Young Plan

The Young Plan is an agreement with the Western powers to reduce Germany's reparation payments and give us more fiscal autonomy. Simultaneously, France will agree to withdraw its military occupation from the Rhineland.

While this seems to be a positive development for the country, the Right is campaigning hard against this plan, as are the Communists for whatever reason. They claim that any reparations are a form of national slavery, and have organized a referendum against it.

- @pro_plan: Campaign in favor of the Young Plan and against the referendum.
- @no_plan: Do not campaign on the Young Plan, one way or another.

@pro_plan

How should we campaign in favor of the Plan?

- @internationalism: As part of a broader campaign in favor of internationalism and pacifism.
- @rational: The Young Plan is simply the most rational choice for Germany.

@internationalism
go-to: marx if president == "Marx"
on-arrival: nationalism -= 5*(1-dissent) if pacifism >= 2 else nationalism += 3; pacifism += 1; workers_spd += 5*(1-dissent) if pacifism >= 3 and nationalism <= 50; workers_nsdap += 4 if pacifism <= 3; rural_nsdap += 5; catholics_spd -= 4 if pacifism <= 3; rural_dvp -= 4

We rail hard against nationalism and in favor of pacifism and belonging to the international community of nations. The referendum easily fails, with only around 15% of voters supporting it. It seems that nationalism is not omnipotent in Germany, despite everything. [? if pacifism >= 3 and nationalism <= 50 : We have rallied the workers to the cause of internationalism. ?]


@rational
go-to: marx if president == "Marx"
on-arrival: nationalism += 5; workers_nsdap += 4; rural_nsdap += 5; catholics_spd -= 4; workers_spd -= 3; rural_dvp -= 5

The referendum easily fails, with only around 15% of voters supporting it. It seems that the German people have a sense of rationality, after all.


@no_plan
go-to: marx if president == "Marx"
on-arrival: nationalism += 5; workers_spd -= 3; old_middle_spd -= 3; new_middle_spd -= 3; pacifism -= 1; workers_nsdap += 5; rural_nsdap += 5; rural_dnvp -= 5; catholics_spd -= 5; rural_dvp -= 5;

The referendum easily fails with or without our presence in the campaign, with only around 15% of voters supporting it. However, nationalist sentiment is inflammed, and the right-wing parties are using our silence around the Plan as a tacit admission of its faults. Our silence has only emboldened the Right, especially the NSDAP.

@marx
on-arrival: workers_nsdap += 5; new_middle_nsdap += 10; old_middle_nsdap += 10; rural_nsdap += 10; unemployed_nsdap += 5; new_middle_dnvp += 5; old_middle_dnvp += 5; rural_dnvp += 5; new_middle_dvp -= 5; new_middle_other -= 5; old_middle_dvp -= 5; old_middle_other -= 5; rural_dvp -= 5; rural_other -= 5

However, the referendum has succeeded in acting as a wedge issue against the moderate bourgeois parties, and the pendelum has swung significantly to the right.

@young_plan_right_coalition

= The Young Plan and the fall of the coalition

The Foreign Ministry under Gustav Streseman has agreed to the Young Plan, an agreement with the Western powers to reduce Germany's reparation payments and give us more fiscal autonomy. Simultaneously, France will agree to withdraw its military occupation from the Rhineland.

While this seems to be a positive development for the country, the DNVP (and especially its leader, Alfred Hugenberg) opposes the plan, claiming that any reparations are a form of national slavery. They have called for a vote of no confidence against the government, supported by the NSDAP and the USPD, and for a referendum on the Young Plan.

We can either vote to bring down the government and hold new elections, or "tolerate" a government led by the remaining bourgeois parties.

- @vonc_yes
- @vonc_no
- @no_matter

@vonc_yes
title: Support the vote of no confidence, voting against the government.
subtitle: The government will collapse, and there may be new elections.
view-if: neo_weimar_coalition >= 50
on-arrival: do_the_thing_after_this = 1 if president == "Marx"; spd_in_government = 0; in_right_coalition = 0; in_grand_coalition = 0; spd_toleration = 0; dvp_relation -= 5; z_relation -= 5;
go-to: marx_right if president == "Marx"; thing_did if president != "Marx"

The right-wing coalition has fallen. If a new one cannot be formed, [+ president +] is likely to dissolve the Reichstag for new elections.

@thing_did

- @enter_government: We will enter government.
- @new_elections: There will be new elections.

@enter_government
choose-if: grand_coalition >= 50 and (z_relation >= 45 or z_party_leader == "Joos") and (dvp_relation >= 30 or stresemann_dead == 0)
subtitle: SPD + Z + BVP + DDP + DVP ([ + grand_coalition +]%)
unavailable-subtitle: SPD + Z + BVP + DDP + DVP ([+ grand_coalition +]%) - [? if grand_coalition < 50 : We do not have the votes. ?][? if (z_relation < 45 and z_party_leader != Joos) or (dvp_relation < 30 and stresemann_dead == 1) : The right would rather see their government fall than let us into government. ?]
go-to: election_1928.grand_coalition_z_lead

We have entered government and taken the DNVP's place.

@new_elections
subtitle: With the Reichstag hung, [+ president +] will dissolve it
on-arrival: time_to_election = 3; pro_republic -= 3; z_relation -= 2; dvp_relation -= 3; marx_relation -= 5
call: set_next_election_time

The Reichstag has been dissolved, as there is no clear governing majority.

@vonc_no
title: Support the rump Center-led government, voting in favor of the government.
subtitle: We would essentially provide "toleration" to a bourgeois government.
view-if: neo_weimar_coalition >= 50
on-arrival: spd_toleration = 1; in_right_coalition = 0; left_dissent += 8; 
go-to: marx_right if president == "Marx"

By supporting the government, we have essentially entered into a "toleration" arrangement with the [+ chancellor +] government. We do not have a voice in the government, but we are responsible for its continued stability. The left of our party opposes this plan, and would rather that we force new elections.

@no_matter
title: It does not matter what we do.
subtitle: The anti-government parties have over 50% of the vote, no matter our choices.
view-if: neo_weimar_coalition < 50
call: set_next_election_time
on-arrival: time_to_election = 3; spd_in_government = 0; in_right_coalition = 0; in_grand_coalition = 0; spd_toleration = 0; pro_republic -= 5
go-to: marx_right if president == "Marx"

The right-wing coalition has fallen. New elections have been set for [+ next_election_month : month +] [+ next_election_year +].

@marx_right
on-arrival: workers_nsdap += 5; new_middle_nsdap += 10; old_middle_nsdap += 10; rural_nsdap += 10; unemployed_nsdap += 5; new_middle_dnvp += 5; old_middle_dnvp += 5; rural_dnvp += 5; new_middle_dvp -= 5; new_middle_other -= 5; old_middle_dvp -= 5; old_middle_other -= 5; rural_dvp -= 5; rural_other -= 5
go-to: thing_did if do_the_thing_after_this

Regardless, the Young Plan has successfully acted as a wedge issue against the moderate bourgeois parties, and the pendelum has swung significantly to the right in this crisis.
